---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Section from '../Section.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../SectionHeading.astro';
import headshot from '../../assets/headshot.jpg';
---

<Section id="about" class="bg-porcelain py-24 md:py-32 lg:py-40">
  <SectionHeading number="05">
    My path began on the water.
  </SectionHeading>

  <div class="mt-14 grid grid-cols-12 gap-x-6 gap-y-12 lg:mt-20">
    <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-5">
      <div class="relative aspect-[4/3] overflow-hidden lg:aspect-[3/4]" data-reveal-scale>
        <Image
          src={headshot}
          alt="Mark Stephens, estate manager and former boat captain"
          widths={[640, 960]}
          sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 38vw, 100vw"
          class="h-full w-full object-cover object-top"
        />
      </div>
      <p class="eyebrow mt-5 text-ink/50">Mark Stephens</p>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink/60">Owner &amp; Estate Manager</p>
    </div>

    <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-6 lg:col-start-7" data-reveal>
      <p class="display-sub max-w-xl text-xl leading-relaxed text-ink/85 md:text-2xl" data-scroll-text>
        For many years, I worked as a boat captain, navigating vessels where precision, foresight, and
        responsibility were not optional — they were the standard.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-8 max-w-xl space-y-6 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-ink/70">
        <p>
          I was born in San Diego into a Navy family and raised on Bainbridge Island, Washington, surrounded by
          evergreen forests and cold saltwater. The pull of sun and open water eventually carried me to Hawaii,
          where I found surfing — and where the ocean quietly set the course for everything that followed. I
          earned my captain&rsquo;s seat at twenty-four, refined my craft at Seattle Maritime Academy, and was
          pursuing a captain&rsquo;s position aboard private yachts when an unexpected opportunity arose on land
          — a different kind of vessel to steward. What I often call the &ldquo;land yacht&rdquo; became my next
          chapter.
        </p>
        <p>
          Back on Maui, estate and property management felt like a natural evolution. For fifteen years I
          stewarded a vast estate in Kipahulu, Hawai&#699;i, guiding raw land into a thriving botanical
          sanctuary. The scale changed, but the principles remained: protection of assets, operational
          excellence, thoughtful oversight, and hands-on leadership. From full property transformations and
          ground-up builds to landscape design, budgeting, vendor coordination, and long-term maintenance, I am
          present in every layer of the work.
        </p>
        <p class="display-sub text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink/80">
          To me, estate management is stewardship — ensuring that beauty, function, and value move in quiet
          harmony.
        </p>
      </div>

      <dl class="mt-12 grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 border-t border-ink/15 pt-8 sm:grid-cols-3">
        <div>
          <dt class="eyebrow text-ink/50">Foresight</dt>
          <dd class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink/65">Solving problems before they appear.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="eyebrow text-ink/50">Integrity</dt>
          <dd class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink/65">An unwavering standard of excellence.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="eyebrow text-ink/50">Stewardship</dt>
          <dd class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink/65">Hands-on leadership, in every layer of the work.</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </div>
</Section>
